  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fish Right Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fish Right is a partnership between the Government of the Philippines and the U.S. Agency for International Development to improve marine biodiversity and the fisheries sector in three key ecological areas. The program will be implemented by the Coastal Resources Center at the University of Rhode Island (URI) in collaboration with a team of core implementing partners, which were selected for their complementary expertise. This program was developed through a consultative process that involved all implementing partners as well as local stakeholders and government representatives.</narrative>
  </description>
